# Every image builds with the repo root as its context (the Dockerfiles say so), so this
# is the only .dockerignore Docker reads. A pattern without `**/` matches at the root only;
# the ones below match at any depth, so nothing a package directory holds locally
# (backend/.env, backend/uploads, a stray node_modules) reaches a build.

# Dependencies and build output: the images install and build their own.
**/node_modules
**/build
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.nyc_output
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment files and secrets. The images take configuration at run time
# (compose environment and Docker secrets), never from the build context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/secrets
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx

# Runtime data a local run leaves behind: database files, uploads (receipts, account
# images), backups, logs, temp files.
data
**/uploads
**/backups
**/logs
**/temp
**/tmp
**/*.log
**/*.tmp
**/*.temp

# Repository metadata, docs, editor and agent files: no image uses them.
**/.git
**/.gitignore
.github
.claude
.design-sync
docs
**/*.md
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~

# OS files
**/.DS_Store
**/._*
**/.Spotlight-V100
**/.Trashes
**/ehthumbs.db
**/Thumbs.db
